WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.286
The bounds hold with probability at least one minus
two over N.

00:00:04.366 --> 00:00:07.474
The upper bound decays at a log-N-over-N rate,

00:00:07.554 --> 00:00:10.523
faster than the square-root Rademacher rate.

00:00:10.603 --> 00:00:14.195
Variance scales as noise times twice the rank over N.

00:00:14.275 --> 00:00:19.670
And these are the first finite-rank bounds with a
high-probability lower bound.
